      "text": [
        "5632 - وَ رَوَى اَلْحَسَنُ بْنُ مَحْبُوبٍ عَنْ عَلِيِّ بْنِ رِئَابٍ عَنْ أَبِي عُبَيْدَةَ عَنْ أَبِي جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ :\nفِي رَجُلٍ مَاتَ وَ تَرَكَ اِمْرَأَتَهُ وَ أُخْتَهُ وَ جَدَّهُ فَقَالَ \"هَذِهِ مِنْ أَرْبَعَةِ أَسْهُمٍ لِلْمَرْأَةِ اَلرُّبُعُ وَ لِلْأُخْتِ سَهْمٌ وَ لِلْجَدِّ سَهْمَانِ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5632 - Al-Hasan ibn Mahbub narrated from Ali ibn Riʾab from Abu Ubaydah from Abu Jafar (as) regarding a man who passed away and left behind his wife, his sister, and his grandfather.\nImam (as) said: \"This inheritance is divided into four shares: the wife receives one-fourth, the sister receives one share, and the grandfather receives two shares.\""
        ]
      }
